    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16945" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτάλαντος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰτᾰ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span> copul., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τάλαντον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>equal in weight, equivalent
				to, like,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. Ἄρηϊ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.576
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διῒ μῆτιν ἀ.</span>
			<i>equal to</i> Zeus in wisdom, <i><span class="en">
				2.169
			</span></i>, etc.: generally, <i>like,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀστέρι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.40
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>in equipoise,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				22
			</span></i>.</div>
